	(text "Layout (#86): D5 (USB_DP), D6 (USB_DM), D7 (VBUS_USB) right\nat the J10 pins, before any other part on the line (C32, D8, U2).\nShort, direct GND via at each diode anode (pin 2).\nRoute USB_DP/USB_DM as a pair J10 -> U2 PA12/PA11;\ntrace runs over the D5/D6 pads, no stubs.\nJ10 shell (pad 1) to the GND plane with short connections.\nGeneral knowledge: D68 (H5VUD5U) gives ratings and pads only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 123.19 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left top)
		)
		(uuid "5d1e8c47-2a9b-4f63-8e05-7c3b9a6d2f18")
	)
	(text "USB-C device, USB FS on PA11/PA12. CC1/CC2 5.1k to GND (sink).\nVBUS_USB -> D8 SS14 -> U8 XC6206 3.3V -> +3V3, so the MCU runs from USB alone.\nD8 stops +3V3 back-driving VBUS through U8 when only the 24V PSU is on.\nD10 (anode +3V3, cathode LDO_IN) holds U8 VOUT <= VIN + 0.3V (D69 p3 abs max) when +3V3 comes from the buck and USB is off (issue #67).\nUSB only: +3V3 back-feeds the TPS5430 output; +24V sits near 2.7V (accepted, issue #1).\nFirmware (plan 4.5 USB limits, #56, #78): cap the backlight PWM at 20 % duty and hold BUZZER (PB15) low whenever U8 may carry the load:\nVBUS_SENSE shows no PSU, or a USB host has enumerated the board (also with the PSU on). U8 is 200 mA, 250 mW in SOT-23 (D69 p1, p3).\nBudget (#81): 1.72 V max across U8; 97 mA without backlight, 177 mA at 100 % (303 mW, over), 113 mA at 20 % (193 mW)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 30.48 160.02 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "b44a27e9-3dbf-488b-9488-f16375293298")
	)
